# covers: 2 Recursive types
# covers: 6 Recursive data structures
# covers: 2 Maps / Dictionaries
# covers: 8 Collection iteration
# covers: 2 Type aliases
# kind: positive
# expect: run
# exit: 0
# stdout: 7
# stdout: x
# stdout: y

trees is module
trees purpose "Build the tree for (1 + 2) + x in a node list, evaluate it by recursion against a symbol table, and list the table"
trees path trees
trees imports standard.console
trees imports standard.list
trees imports standard.map
trees imports standard.math
trees exports main

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter purpose "Authority to write lines to standard output"
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout none

Operands is record
Operands purpose "The two operands of a sum node, by their positions in the node list"
Operands typeParameter none
Operands field left NodeId
Operands field right NodeId

Expr is enum
Expr purpose "One node of an expression tree: a number, a name, or the sum of two other nodes"
Expr typeParameter none
Expr variant number Int64
Expr variant name String
Expr variant sum Operands

Nodes is typeInstance
Nodes purpose "The nodes of an expression tree, in the order they were added"
Nodes instantiates list.List Expr

NodeId is alias
NodeId purpose "The position of a node in a Nodes list, received when the node is added"
NodeId typeParameter none
NodeId aliasOf Int64
NodeId indexes Nodes

Symbols is typeInstance
Symbols purpose "The value of each defined name, in the order the names were first defined"
Symbols instantiates map.Map String Int64

EvalError is enum
EvalError purpose "Why an expression could not be evaluated"
EvalError typeParameter none
EvalError variant unknownName none
EvalError variant missingNode Int64

evaluate is operation
evaluate purpose "Evaluate the tree whose root is at a position, operands first, by recursion"
evaluate invariant none
evaluate typeParameter none
evaluate input nodes Nodes borrowed
evaluate input symbols Symbols borrowed
evaluate input at NodeId copied
evaluate output Int64
evaluate outputOwnedBy none
evaluate raises EvalError
evaluate effect none
evaluate uses none
evaluate memoryHeap false
evaluate async false
evaluate maxRecursion 16
evaluate label begin loopKind none
evaluate label begin within none
evaluate label missing loopKind none
evaluate label missing within none
evaluate label reportMissing loopKind none
evaluate label reportMissing within none
evaluate label inspect loopKind none
evaluate label inspect within none
evaluate label isNumber loopKind none
evaluate label isNumber within none
evaluate label isName loopKind none
evaluate label isName within none
evaluate label found loopKind none
evaluate label found within none
evaluate label unknown loopKind none
evaluate label unknown within none
evaluate label isSum loopKind none
evaluate label isSum within none
evaluate label sumSecond loopKind none
evaluate label sumSecond within none
evaluate label sumBoth loopKind none
evaluate label sumBoth within none
evaluate label passLeft loopKind none
evaluate label passLeft within none
evaluate label passRight loopKind none
evaluate label passRight within none
evaluate let none
evaluate at begin do readNode
evaluate at begin branch ifError readNode goto missing else goto inspect
evaluate at missing match readError list.IndexOutOfRange
evaluate at missing case list.IndexOutOfRange.outOfRange bind badPosition Int64 goto reportMissing
evaluate at reportMissing do makeMissing
evaluate at reportMissing return error missingError
evaluate at inspect match node Expr
evaluate at inspect case Expr.number bind number Int64 goto isNumber
evaluate at inspect case Expr.name bind text String goto isName
evaluate at inspect case Expr.sum bind operands Operands goto isSum
evaluate at isNumber return ok number
evaluate at isName do lookUp
evaluate at isName branch ifError lookUp goto unknown else goto found
evaluate at found return ok named
evaluate at unknown do makeUnknown
evaluate at unknown return error unknownError
evaluate at isSum do leftId
evaluate at isSum do evaluateLeft
evaluate at isSum branch ifError evaluateLeft goto passLeft else goto sumSecond
evaluate at sumSecond do rightId
evaluate at sumSecond do evaluateRight
evaluate at sumSecond branch ifError evaluateRight goto passRight else goto sumBoth
evaluate at sumBoth do addBoth
evaluate at sumBoth return ok total
evaluate at passLeft return error leftError
evaluate at passRight return error rightError

